<title>ITALY: No EU country has assured entry to EMU yet - Monti.</title>
<headline>No EU country has assured entry to EMU yet - Monti.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>No European country has a guaranteed entry into the future single European currency at the moment even if they are making great efforts to meet the EMU goals, EU Commissioner Mario Monti told reporters here.</p>
<p>Monti, speaking on the fringe of a Global 24 Hour European Monetary Conference, was asked about the risk of France being left out due to its deficit to gross domestic product (GDP) level.</p>
<p>Monti said: &quot;The dangers are ever present. No country has at the moment a guaranteed entry into EMU even if they are all making very intense efforts to meet the requirements.&quot;</p>
<p>He said Italy had good intentions and he was sure it would do everything necessary to reach the goal.</p>
<p>--Milan bureau +39 2 66129507</p>
</text>
